  "nl_text": "This database schema, named schemabench_0150, is used to store information for a social news aggregation website. It contains 15 tables, each representing a different entity or relationship in the system.\nThe moderations table stores information about moderation actions taken on stories, such as banning or deleting comments. It has columns for the moderator's user ID, the story ID, the comment ID, the reason for the moderation action, the suggested action, and the date and time of the moderation.\nThe tags table stores information about tags that can be applied to stories. It has columns for the tag ID, the tag name, the description, and the date and time the tag was created.\nThe story_tags table stores information about which tags have been applied to which stories. It has columns for the story ID, the tag ID, and the date and time the tag was applied.\nThe saved_stories table stores information about which stories have been saved by which users. It has columns for the user ID, the story ID, and the date and time the story was saved.\nThe domains table stores information about the domains that are allowed to post stories. It has columns for the domain ID, the domain name, the date and time the domain was created, and a flag indicating whether the domain is banned.\nThe votes table stores information about which users have voted on which stories and comments. It has columns for the user ID, the story ID, the comment ID, the vote (1 for upvote, -1 for downvote), and the date and time the vote was cast.\nThe invitations table stores information about invitations that have been sent to users to join the website. It has columns for the invitation ID, the user ID, the email address, the date and time the invitation was sent, and the date and time the invitation was used.\nThe messages table stores information about messages that have been sent between users. It has columns for the message ID, the sender ID, the recipient ID, the subject, the body, the date and time the message was sent, a flag indicating whether the message has been read, and a flag indicating whether the message has been deleted by either the sender or the recipient.\nThe moderation_logs table stores information about moderation actions taken on stories, such as banning or deleting comments. It has columns for the moderation ID, the story ID, the user ID, the action taken, and the date and time the action was taken.\nThe ar_internal_metadata table stores information about the internal metadata of the database. It has columns for the key, the value, the date and time the key was created, and the date and time the key was updated.\nThe schema_migrations table stores information about the schema migrations that have been applied to the database. It has columns for the version.\nThe stories table stores information about the stories that have been posted to the website. It has columns for the story ID, the user ID, the title, the description, the URL, the date and time the story was created, the date and time the story was updated, a flag indicating whether the story has been moderated, and the score.\nThe hidden_stories table stores information about which stories have been hidden by which users. It has columns for the user ID, the story ID, and the date and time the story was hidden.\nThe users table stores information about the users who have registered on the website. It has columns for the user ID, the username, the email address, the encrypted password, the password digest, the date and time the user was created, the date and time the user was updated, the settings, a flag indicating whether the user is banned, and a flag indicating whether the user is an admin.\nThe comments table stores information about the comments that have been posted on stories. It has columns for the comment ID, the story ID, the user ID, the body, the date and time the comment was created, the date and time the comment was updated, and a flag indicating whether the comment has been deleted.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project involves the development of a technology-focused community platform for link aggregation and discussion, similar to Hacker News. The platform, named Lobsters, is designed to cater primarily to enthusiasts and professionals in technology, programming, and computer science. It operates with an invite-only model to ensure high-quality content and discourse.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To provide a platform for sharing and discussing links related to technology, programming, and computer science.\n- To maintain a high standard of content quality through an invite-only membership system.\n- To enhance community transparency with a public moderation log.\n- To facilitate community replication by operating as open-source software.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Community Members: Users who submit links and participate in discussions.\n- Moderators: Users responsible for content moderation and maintaining community standards.\n- Administrators: Users with elevated privileges to manage platform operations.\n- Visitors: Non-members who can view content but not participate.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Registration and Management: Support for invite-based user registration and profile management.\n- Content Submission: Users can submit links to articles, research papers, and blog posts.\n- Discussion Threads: Users can engage in threaded discussions related to submitted content.\n- Voting System: Users can vote on stories and comments to influence content visibility.\n- Tagging System: Stories can be tagged for improved categorization and searchability.\n- Story Moderation: Tools for moderators to manage content quality, including moderation logs.\n- Messaging System: Direct messaging capabilities for communication between members.\n- Story and Comment Management: Functions for saving, hiding, and moderating stories and comments.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The platform should efficiently support growth in user base and content volume.\n- Security: Implementation of robust security measures, including encrypted passwords and data protection.\n- Performance: Ensuring low latency for user interactions, even with increased load.\n- Transparency: Access to public moderation logs to uphold community standards.\n- Usability: Intuitive user interface and navigation to promote ease of use.\n- Open-Source Accessibility: Available for other communities to replicate and adapt.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0150.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0150\nCREATE TABLE `moderations` (\n  `moderation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `moderator_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reason` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `suggested_action` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`moderation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `moderations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`moderator_user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderations_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `tag_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tag_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `story_tags` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `applied_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`, `tag_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `story_tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `story_tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `tags` (`tag_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `saved_stories` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `saved_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `saved_stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `saved_stories_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `domains` (\n  `domain_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `domain_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_banned` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`domain_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `votes` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vote` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `voted_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `story_id`, `comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `invitations` (\n  `invitation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sent_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `used_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invitation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invitations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `messages` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recipient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subject` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `sent_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_read` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `is_deleted` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recipient_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `moderation_logs` (\n  `moderation_log_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `action_taken` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`moderation_log_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `moderation_logs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderation_logs_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `ar_internal_metadata` (\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`key`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `schema_migrations` (\n  `version` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`version`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `stories` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_moderated` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `hidden_stories` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hidden_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `hidden_stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `hidden_stories_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `encrypted_password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_digest` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `settings` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_banned` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `is_admin` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `is_deleted` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
